"Let $H$ be a graph, and let $\\operatorname{ex}_{\\mathcal{P}}(n,H,\\emptyset)$ denote the maximum number of copies of $H$ in an $n$-vertex planar graph.\n\n**Eppstein's conjecture.** For every graph $H$, there exists a non-negative integer $k$ such that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ex}_{\\mathcal{P}}(n,H,\\emptyset)=\\Theta(n^k).\n$$\n\nThis is a restricted planar version of a question posed by Eppstein about subgraph counts in minor-closed graph families. The paper presents it as an open conjecture, while verifying it for trees and establishing general upper bounds."